('127.58.d.16.G',4,'Regional soil loss can affect global food supply by:','["Having no effect", "Replacing food", "Increasing it always", "Reducing crop production"]'::jsonb,3,'Soil underpins food systems.','original'),
('127.58.d.17.A',3,'A watershed is the land area that:','["Drains to a common stream or river", "Never drains", "Has no water", "Is always flat"]'::jsonb,0,'Watersheds collect runoff.','original'),
('127.58.d.17.A',4,'Characteristics of a local watershed include:','["Brand names", "Land use, slope, and stream flow", "Phone numbers", "Paint colors"]'::jsonb,1,'They describe how water moves.','original'),
('127.58.d.17.B',3,'Urbanization increases flooding because pavement:','["Cools the soil", "Absorbs water", "Prevents water from soaking in", "Grows plants"]'::jsonb,2,'Impervious surfaces raise runoff.','original'),
('127.58.d.17.B',4,'A drought can lower stream flow and:','["Cool the water", "Raise water quality", "Increase aquifers", "Stress irrigation supplies"]'::jsonb,3,'Dry spells limit water.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.A',3,'Soil and plants are interrelated because plants:','["Stabilize soil and add organic matter", "Never need soil", "Remove all soil", "Create rocks"]'::jsonb,0,'Plants protect and build soil.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.A',4,'Soil supports plants by providing:','["Only light", "Anchorage, water, air, and nutrients", "Only sound", "Only heat"]'::jsonb,1,'Soil meets plant needs.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.B',3,'Compared with agricultural soils, urban soils are often:','["Always fertile", "Deeper and richer", "Compacted and disturbed", "Untouched"]'::jsonb,2,'Construction compacts soil.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.B',4,'Urban soils often have lower organic matter because of:','["Extra compost", "Natural forests", "More worms", "Removal of topsoil during development"]'::jsonb,3,'Development strips topsoil.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.C',3,'Hydroponics is growing plants in:','["Nutrient solution instead of soil", "Pure sand", "Dry air", "Dirt only"]'::jsonb,0,'Roots sit in solution.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.C',4,'In a hydroponic system the solution must be monitored for:','["Brand", "Nutrient concentration and pH", "Color", "Sunset times"]'::jsonb,1,'Control of the solution is critical.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.D',3,'An advantage of hydroponics is that it:','["Needs no light", "Uses more water", "Uses less water and allows controlled nutrition", "Is always free"]'::jsonb,2,'Efficient resource use.','original'),
('127.58.d.18.D',4,'A disadvantage of hydroponics is that it:','["Never fails", "Costs nothing", "Needs no care", "Can have high startup costs and needs close monitoring"]'::jsonb,3,'Systems need investment.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.A',3,'Cotton in Texas begins its life cycle with:','["Planting seed in warm soil", "Drying", "Harvest", "Ginning"]'::jsonb,0,'Planting starts the cycle.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.A',4,'A major Texas crop that thrives in the High Plains with irrigation is:','["Maple", "Cotton", "Cranberries", "Cocoa"]'::jsonb,1,'The High Plains grows lots of cotton.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.B',3,'Plant breeding uses genetics to:','["Stop evolution", "Remove genes", "Select plants with desired traits as parents", "Ignore traits"]'::jsonb,2,'Breeding combines traits.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.B',4,'Crossing a high-yield plant with a disease-resistant plant aims to produce:','["Identical clones", "No seeds", "Weaker plants", "Offspring with both traits"]'::jsonb,3,'Breeders combine desirable traits.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.C',3,'A new crop variety that took many years of selection and testing shows:','["Plant breeding takes time", "No testing", "Instant results", "Luck"]'::jsonb,0,'Development is slow.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.C',4,'Field trials of new varieties help breeders to:','["Avoid farmers", "Compare performance across locations", "Skip testing", "Reduce data"]'::jsonb,1,'Trials give evidence.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.D',3,'A student testing inheritance of flower color in peas would:','["Paint flowers", "Guess", "Cross parents and count offspring phenotypes", "Skip counting"]'::jsonb,2,'Experiments test genetics.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.D',4,'A ratio of about 3 purple to 1 white offspring from two hybrid parents supports:','["Blending", "Mutation only", "No genetics", "Dominant and recessive inheritance"]'::jsonb,3,'3:1 is Mendelian.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.E',3,'An alternative growing method such as aquaponics combines:','["Fish and plant production", "Soil and rock", "Cattle and wheat", "Trees and sand"]'::jsonb,0,'Fish waste feeds plants.','original'),
('127.58.d.19.E',4,'Testing a hydroponic lettuce system against soil-grown lettuce compares:','["Pot colors", "Growth rate, water use, and yield", "Slogans", "Names"]'::jsonb,1,'Fair tests compare results.','original'),
('127.56.d.3.A',3,'A chapter member who chairs a committee for a vineyard field day is developing:','["Spectator habits", "Weaker teamwork", "Leadership and organizing skills", "Fewer duties"]'::jsonb,2,'Chairing builds leadership.','original'),
('127.57.d.3.A',2,'Which action shows leadership in an advanced floral class?','["Leaving early", "Ignoring deadlines", "Avoiding group tasks", "Coordinating teammates on a large event order"]'::jsonb,3,'Coordinating others builds leadership.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
